class=\"item\">\n   255→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   256→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span>\n   257→                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   258→                    </div>\n   259→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   260→                        Automations, Cloud Agents, Bugbot Improvements, Design Mode Updates\n   261→                    </div>\n   262→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   263→                        2025-06-22 | <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Details</a>\n   264→                    </div>\n   265→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   266→                        /automate skill for creating automations directly in agent sessions, new GitHub and Slack triggers, cloud environment setup, cloud subagents with /in-cloud, improved handoff between local and cloud, and significant Bugbot performance improvements (3x faster, 22% cheaper, 10% more bugs found). Design Mode received multi-select elements and voice input capabilities.\n   267→                    </div>\n   268→                </div>\n   269→\n   270→                <div class=\"item\">\n   271→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   272→                        <span class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n   273→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   274→                    </div>\n   275→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   276→                        MCP Support Generally Available in VS Code (v1.102)\n   277→                    </div>\n   278→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   279→                        2025-07-09 | <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2025-07-15-github-copilot-in-vs-code-june-release-v1-102/\" target=\"_blank\">View Details</a>\n   280→                    </div>\n   281→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   282→                        Model Context Protocol (MCP) support generally available in the June 2025 VS Code release (v1.102). Includes open-sourced Copilot Chat extension and support for Copilot coding agent.\n   283→                    </div>\n   284→                </div>\n   285→\n   286→                <div class=\"item\">\n   287→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   288→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Aider</span>\n   289→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   290→                    </div>\n   291→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   292→                        v0.85.0 - Responses API Models and Gemini 2.5 Support\n   293→                    </div>\n   294→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   295→                        2025-06-27 | <a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\" target=\"_blank\">View Details</a>\n   296→                    </div>\n   297→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   298→                        Support for OpenAI's Responses API models (o1-pro, o3-pro), new Gemini 2.5 Pro models, updated o3 pricing, thinking tokens support, and quality-of-life improvements. Aider wrote 21% of the code in this release.\n   299→                    </div>\n   300→                </div>\n   301→\n   302→                <div class=\"item\">\n   303→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   304→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf</span>\n   305→                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   306→                    </div>\n   307→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   308→                        Claude 3.7 Sonnet Support and Team Model Controls\n   309→                    </div>\n   310→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   311→                        2025-03-17 | <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog/vscode\" target=\"_blank\">View Details</a>\n   312→                    </div>\n   313→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   314→                        Added Claude 3.7 Sonnet model support and introduced model selection controls for teams and enterprise plans, allowing admins to select which models are available to team members.\n   315→                    </div>\n   316→                </div>\n   317→\n   318→                <div class=\"item\">\n   319→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   320→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Devin</span>\n   321→                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   322→                    </div>\n   323→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   324→                        Windows VM Support and Improved Feedback Controls\n   325→                    </div>\n   326→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   327→                        2025-06-01 | <a href=\"https://cognition.ai/blog\" target=\"_blank\">View Details</a>\n   328→                    </div>\n   329→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   330→                        Expanded to support building, running, and testing natively in Windows VMs. Introduced improved feedback controls with always-visible thumbs-up/down buttons and enhanced session-level feedback modal.\n   331→                    </div>\n   332→                </div>\n   333→\n   334→                <div class=\"item\">\n   335→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   336→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span>\n   337→                        <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Note</span>\n   338→                    </div>\n   339→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   340→                        No specific updates in June 2025 timeframe\n   341→                    </div>\n   342→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   343→                        2025-06-01 | <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Details</a>\n   344→                    </div>\n   345→                </div>\n   346→\n   347→                <div class=\"item\">\n   348→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   349→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Continue</span>\n   350→                        <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Note</span>\n   351→                    </div>\n   352→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   353→                        Acquired by Cursor - No Active June 2025 Updates\n   354→                    </div>\n   355→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   356→                        2025-06-01 | <a href=\"https://changelog.continue.dev/\" target=\"_blank\">View Details</a>\n   357→                    </div>\n   358→                </div>\n   359→            </section>\n   360→\n   361→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   362→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   363→                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   364→\n   365→                <div class=\"item\">\n   366→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   367→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27009\" target=\"_blank\">Semantic Early-Stopping for Iterative LLM Agent Loops</a>\n   368→                    </div>\n   369→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   370→                        Halts loops when consecutive draft embeddings stop changing in meaning\n   371→                    </div>\n   372→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   373→                        Sahil Shrivastava | 2026-06-26\n   374→                    </div>\n   375→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   376→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM agents</span>\n   377→                        <span class=\"topic\">early stopping</span>\n   378→                    </div>\n   379→                </div>\n   380→\n   381→                <div class=\"item\">\n   382→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   383→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27136\" target=\"_blank\">Joint Learning of Experiential Rules and Policies</a>\n   384→                    </div>\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   386→                        Framework for jointly learning experiential rules and policies for LLM agents\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   389→                        Shicheng Ye, Chao Yu | 2026-06-26\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   392→                        <span class=\"topic\">experiential learning</span>\n   393→                        <span class=\"topic\">policy learning</span>\n   394→                    </div>\n   395→                </div>\n   396→\n   397→                <div class=\"item\">\n   398→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   399→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27226\" target=\"_blank\">Ask, Don't Judge: Binary Questions for LLM Evaluation</a>\n   400→                    </div>\n   401→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   402→                        Using binary questions for more interpretable LLM evaluation and self-improvement\n   403→                    </div>\n   404→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   405→                        Sangwoo Cho et al. | 2026-06-26\n   406→                    </div>\n   407→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   408→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM evaluation</span>\n   409→                        <span class=\"topic\">interpretability</span>\n   410→                    </div>\n   411→                </div>\n   412→\n   413→                <div class=\"item\">\n   414→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   415→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27287\" target=\"_blank\">Prompt Injection in Automated Résumé Screening</a>\n   416→                    </div>\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   418→                        Analyzes prompt injection vulnerabilities in résumé screening systems using LLMs\n   419→                    </div>\n   420→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   421→                        Preet Baxi et al. | 2026-06-26\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   424→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM security</span>\n   425→                        <span class=\"topic\">prompt injection</span>\n   426→                    </div>\n   427→                </div>\n   428→\n   429→                <div class=\"item\">\n   430→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   431→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26935\" target=\"_blank\">Where Do CoT Training Gains Land?</a>\n   432→                    </div>\n   433→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   434→                        Investigates Chain-of-Thought reasoning in language-model agents\n   435→                    </div>\n   436→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   437→                        Jingyu Liu et al. | 2026-06-26\n   438→                    </div>\n   439→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   440→                        <span class=\"topic\">Chain-of-Thought</span>\n   441→                        <span class=\"topic\">reasoning</span>\n   442→                    </div>\n   443→                </div>\n   444→\n   445→                <div class=\"item\">\n   446→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   447→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26806\" target=\"_blank\">Memory Depth, Not Memory Access</a>\n   448→                    </div>\n   449→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   450→                        Selective parametric consolidation for long-running language agents\n   451→                    </div>\n   452→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   453→                        Haoliang Han | 2026-06-26\n   454→                    </div>\n   455→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   456→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM memory</span>\n   457→                        <span class=\"topic\">parametric consolidation</span>\n   458→                    </div>\n   459→                </div>\n   460→\n   461→                <div class=\"item\">\n   462→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   463→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26649\" target=\"_blank\">Autoformalization of Agent Instructions</a>\n   464→                    </div>\n   465→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   466→                        Translates agent prompts into formalized policy-as-code implementations\n   467→                    </div>\n   468→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   469→                        Adam Mondl et al. | 2026-06-26\n   470→                    </div>\n   471→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   472→                        <span class=\"topic\">autoformalization</span>\n   473→                        <span class=\"topic\">policy-as-code</span>\n   474→                    </div>\n   475→                </div>\n   476→\n   477→                <div class=\"item\">\n   478→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   479→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27288\" target=\"_blank\">Co-Failure Ceiling on Model Combination</a>\n   480→                    </div>\n   481→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   482→                        Studies when combining language models is beneficial across 67 frontier models\n   483→                    </div>\n   484→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   485→                        Josef Chen | 2026-06-26\n   486→                    </div>\n   487→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   488→                        <span class=\"topic\">model combination</span>\n   489→                        <span class=\"topic\">ensemble methods</span>\n   490→                    </div>\n   491→                </div>\n   492→\n   493→                <div class=\"item\">\n   494→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   495→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26859\" target=\"_blank\">AgentX: Self-Iteration of Recommender Systems</a>\n   496→                    </div>\n   497→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   498→                        Agent-driven framework for continuous improvement of recommendation systems\n   499→                    </div>\n   500→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   501→                        Changxin Lao et al. | 2026-06-26\n   502→                    </div>\n   503→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   504→                        <span class=\"topic\">recommender systems</span>\n   505→                        <span class=\"topic\">self-iteration</span>\n   506→                    </div>\n   507→                </div>\n   508→\n   509→                <div class=\"item\">\n   510→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   511→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26918\" target=\"_blank\">Diagnosing Task Insensitivity in Language Agents</a>\n   512→                    </div>\n   513→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   514→                        Diagnostic approaches for task-insensitive behavior in language agents\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   517→                        Jingyu Liu et al. | 2026-06-26\n   518→                    </div>\n   519→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   520→                        <span class=\"topic\">task sensitivity</span>\n   521→                        <span class=\"topic\">agent evaluation</span>\n   522→                    </div>\n   523→                </div>\n   524→\n   525→                <div class=\"item\">\n   526→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   527→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26836\" target=\"_blank\">The Capability Frontier: Benchmarks Miss 82%</a>\n   528→                    </div>\n   529→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   530→                        Argues benchmarks fail to capture 82% of model performance\n   531→                    </div>\n   532→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   533→                        Bradley Fowler et al. | 2026-06-26\n   534→                    </div>\n   535→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   536→                        <span class=\"topic\">benchmarks</span>\n   537→                        <span class=\"topic\">model evaluation</span>\n   538→                    </div>\n   539→                </div>\n   540→\n   541→                <div class=\"item\">\n   542→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   543→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26686\" target=\"_blank\">LeanGuard: Fast and Light Moderation</a>\n   544→                    </div>\n   545→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   546→                        Questions whether safety guardrails need complex reasoning\n   547→                    </div>\n   548→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   549→                        Dongbin Na | 2026-06-26\n   550→                    </div>\n   551→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   552→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI safety</span>\n   553→                        <span class=\"topic\">content moderation</span>\n   554→                    </div>\n   555→                </div>\n   556→\n   557→                <div class=\"item\">\n   558→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   559→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26669\" target=\"_blank\">SKILL-DISCO: Agent Traces to Reusable Skills</a>\n   560→                    </div>\n   561→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   562→                        Distilling and compiling agent traces into reusable procedural skills\n   563→                    </div>\n   564→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   565→                        Zhongxin Guo et al. | 2026-06-26\n   566→                    </div>\n   567→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   568→                        <span class=\"topic\">agent skills</span>\n   569→                        <span class=\"topic\">knowledge distillation</span>\n   570→                    </div>\n   571→                </div>\n   572→\n   573→                <div class=\"item\">\n   574→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   575→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26722\" target=\"_blank\">Socratic Agents for Scientific Discovery</a>\n   576→                    </div>\n   577→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   578→                        Question-driven approaches for autonomous discovery in physical systems\n   579→                    </div>\n   580→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   581→                        Xianrui Zeng et al. | 2026-06-26\n   582→                    </div>\n   583→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   584→                        <span class=\"topic\">scientific discovery</span>\n   585→                        <span class=\"topic\">Socratic methods</span>\n   586→                    </div>\n   587→                </div>\n   588→\n   589→                <div class=\"item\">\n   590→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   591→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26758\" target=\"_blank\">EGG: Expert-Guided Kernel Generation</a>\n   592→                    </div>\n   593→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   594→                        Expert-guided agent framework for efficient kernel generation\n   595→                    </div>\n   596→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   597→                        Yaochen Han et al. | 2026-06-26\n   598→                    </div>\n   599→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   600→                        <span class=\"topic\">kernel generation</span>\n   601→                        <span class=\"topic\">code generation</span>\n   602→                    </div>\n   603→                </div>\n   604→\n   605→                <div class=\"item\">\n   606→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   607→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26502\" target=\"_blank\">Humans Disengage, Reasoning Models Persist</a>\n   608→                    </div>\n   609→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   610→                        Explores how humans vs AI models allocate effort on difficult tasks\n   611→                    </div>\n   612→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   613→                        Han-yu Wang | 2026-06-26\n   614→                    </div>\n   615→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   616→                        <span class=\"topic\">reasoning models</span>\n   617→                        <span class=\"topic\">deliberation</span>\n   618→                    </div>\n   619→                </div>\n   620→\n   621→                <div class=\"item\">\n   622→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   623→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26807\" target=\"_blank\">KARLA: Knowledg