class=\"header-title\">Agentic Coding Research Report</div>\n   316→            <div class=\"header-date\">June 27, 2026</div>\n   317→        </div>\n   318→    </header>\n   319→\n   320→    <div class=\"header-nav\">\n   321→        <a href=\"#overview\">Overview</a> |\n   322→        <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a> |\n   323→        <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Whitelist Updates</a> |\n   324→        <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Technical Insights</a> |\n   325→        <a href=\"#stats\">Statistics</a>\n   326→    </div>\n   327→\n   328→    <div class=\"container\">\n   329→        <main id=\"overview\">\n   330→            <div class=\"highlight-box\">\n   331→                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Top Themes This Week</h2>\n   332→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   333→                    <div class=\"item-title\">1. GPT-5.6 Launch & Government Access (June 26-27)</div>\n   334→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   335→                        OpenAI previews GPT-5.6 series: Sol (flagship), Terra (balanced, 2x cheaper), Luna (fast, affordable).\n   336→                        New pricing model with improved prompt caching. U.S. government to control access decisions.\n   337→                        Major Hacker News discussions (831+ points).\n   338→                    </div>\n   339→                </div>\n   340→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   341→                    <div class=\"item-title\">2. Prompt Injection Defense Progress (June 26)</div>\n   342→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   343→                        6,000 failed hack attempts on OpenClaw challenge. Research shows \"role confusion\" as root vulnerability.\n   344→                        \"Destyling\" attacks reduces success from 61% to 10%. Labs investing in frontier model training against injection.\n   345→                    </div>\n   346→                </div>\n   347→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   348→                    <div class=\"item-title\">3. LLM Agent Research Surge (June 26)</div>\n   349→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   350→                        17 new ArXiv papers on agent systems. Key topics: semantic early-stopping, experiential learning,\n   351→                        memory consolidation. Autoformalization of agent instructions to policy-as-code.\n   352→                        Co-failure ceiling discovered in model combination (67 models studied).\n   353→                    </div>\n   354→                </div>\n   355→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   356→                    <div class=\"item-title\">4. AI Safety & Regulation (June 16-27)</div>\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   358→                        Claude Fable 5 export control controversy (defensive security needs). German ruling: Google liable for\n   359→                        AI overview errors. CVE-2026-LGTM satire highlights multi-agent risks. Vibe coding ethics debates on HN.\n   360→                    </div>\n   361→                </div>\n   362→            </div>\n   363→\n   364→            <div class=\"stats-grid\" id=\"stats\">\n   365→                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   366→                    <div class=\"stat-value\">29</div>\n   367→                    <div class=\"stat-label\">Insights Collected</div>\n   368→                </div>\n   369→                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   370→                    <div class=\"stat-value\">1</div>\n   371→                    <div class=\"stat-label\">New Product</div>\n   372→                </div>\n   373→                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   374→                    <div class=\"stat-value\">0</div>\n   375→                    <div class=\"stat-label\">Whitelist Updates</div>\n   376→                </div>\n   377→                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   378→                    <div class=\"stat-value\">17</div>\n   379→                    <div class=\"stat-label\">ArXiv Papers</div>\n   380→                </div>\n   381→                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   382→                    <div class=\"stat-value\">9</div>\n   383→                    <div class=\"stat-label\">Simon Willison Posts</div>\n   384→                </div>\n   385→                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   386→                    <div class=\"stat-value\">4</div>\n   387→                    <div class=\"stat-label\">HN Discussions</div>\n   388→                </div>\n   389→            </div>\n   390→\n   391→            <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   392→                <section id=\"new-products\">\n   393→                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">\n   394→                        New Products\n   395→                        <span class=\"section-count\">(1)</span>\n   396→                    </h2>\n   397→\n   398→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   399→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   400→                            <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/lukan-ai-agent-ide-and-workstation\" target=\"_blank\">\n   401→                                Lukan AI Agent, IDE and Workstation\n   402→                            </a>\n   403→                        </div>\n   404→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   405→                            Open-source AI workstation that runs on top of your operating system to complete real end-to-end work.\n   406→                            Includes integrated coding agent (built in Rust), tmux-based persistent terminals, multi-agent parallel\n   407→                            execution, and agentic pipelines with approval workflows.\n   408→                        </div>\n   409→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   410→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Product Hunt</span>\n   411→                            Released: 2026-06-23 | Category: AI IDE\n   412→                        </div>\n   413→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   414→                            <span class=\"tag\">Rust</span>\n   415→                            <span class=\"tag\">Multi-Agent</span>\n   416→                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenClaw</span>\n   417→                            <span class=\"tag\">Open Source</span>\n   418→                        </div>\n   419→                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\"The pipeline approvals layer is blocking per-agent but async globally\"</div>\n   420→                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\"Per-step tool access is underappreciated. Most frameworks give the whole pipeline the same permissions\"</div>\n   421→                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\"Persistent memory between sessions - agent barely needs reminding of context\"</div>\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→                </section>\n   424→\n   425→                <section id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   426→                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">\n   427→                        Whitelist Updates\n   428→                        <span class=\"section-count\">(0)</span>\n   429→                    </h2>\n   430→                    <div class=\"empty-state\">\n   431→                        No whitelist updates recorded for this period.\n   432→                    </div>\n   433→                </section>\n   434→\n   435→                <section id=\"technical-insights\">\n   436→                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">\n   437→                        Technical Insights\n   438→                        <span class=\"section-count\">(29)</span>\n   439→                    </h2>\n   440→\n   441→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   442→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   443→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/best\" target=\"_blank\">Hacker News: GPT-5.6 Sol Preview</a>\n   444→                        </div>\n   445→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   446→                            OpenAI's preview of GPT-5.6 Sol as next-generation model. Discussion covers government restrictions\n   447→                            on access - Washington Post reports U.S. government will decide access.\n   448→                        </div>\n   449→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   450→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">HN</span>\n   451→                            831 points | 500+ comments | 2026-06-27\n   452→                        </div>\n   453→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   454→                            <span class=\"tag\">GPT-5.6</span>\n   455→                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>\n   456→                            <span class=\"tag\">Government</span>\n   457→                        </div>\n   458→                    </div>\n   459→\n   460→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   461→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   462→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/best\" target=\"_blank\">AI Assistant Hack Challenge</a>\n   463→                        </div>\n   464→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   465→                            2,000 people tried to hack Fernando Irarrázaval's AI assistant without success.\n   466→                            Highlights community interest in prompt injection defenses and AI security.\n   467→                        </div>\n   468→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   469→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">HN</span>\n   470→                            351 points | 158 comments | 2026-06-27\n   471→                        </div>\n   472→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   473→                            <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n   474→                            <span class=\"tag\">Prompt Injection</span>\n   475→                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenClaw</span>\n   476→                        </div>\n   477→                    </div>\n   478→\n   479→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   480→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   481→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/best\" target=\"_blank\">CVE-2026-LGTM Incident</a>\n   482→                        </div>\n   483→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   484→                            Andrew Nesbitt's satirical AI security incident about competing AI agents entering disagreement loops.\n   485→                            519 points, 83 comments. Highlights multi-agent concerns and inference costs.\n   486→                        </div>\n   487→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   488→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">HN</span>\n   489→                            519 points | 83 comments | 2026-06-27\n   490→                        </div>\n   491→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   492→                            <span class=\"tag\">Multi-Agent</span>\n   493→                            <span class=\"tag\">Satire</span>\n   494→                            <span class=\"tag\">Incident Response</span>\n   495→                        </div>\n   496→                    </div>\n   497→\n   498→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   499→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   500→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/best\" target=\"_blank\">Vibe Coding Controversy</a>\n   501→                        </div>\n   502→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   503→                            Discussion about code attribution and ethics of AI-generated code. \"Hey Nico, you didn't vibe code your\n   504→                            data room but stole it from Papermark.\" 590 points, 275 comments.\n   505→                        </div>\n   506→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   507→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">HN</span>\n   508→                            590 points | 275 comments | 2026-06-27\n   509→                        </div>\n   510→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   511→                            <span class=\"tag\">Ethics</span>\n   512→                            <span class=\"tag\">Attribution</span>\n   513→                            <span class=\"tag\">Vibe Coding</span>\n   514→                        </div>\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→\n   517→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   518→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   519→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">GPT-5.6 Preview and Pricing</a>\n   520→                        </div>\n   521→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   522→                            Three models: Sol (flagship), Terra (2x cheaper), Luna (fast/affordable). Pricing: Sol $5/$30 per 1M tokens,\n   523→                            Terra $2.50/$15, Luna $1/$6. Predictable prompt caching with 30-min cache life.\n   524→                        </div>\n   525→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   526→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n   527→                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-26\n   528→                        </div>\n   529→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   530→                            <span class=\"tag\">GPT-5.6</span>\n   531→                            <span class=\"tag\">Pricing</span>\n   532→                            <span class=\"tag\">Caching</span>\n   533→                        </div>\n   534→                    </div>\n   535→\n   536→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   537→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   538→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Prompt Injection Defense Progress</a>\n   539→                        </div>\n   540→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   541→                            6,000 attempts to leak OpenClaw secrets using Opus 4.6 - zero successes. Anti-prompt-injection rules\n   542→                            and training appear effective. Labs investing in frontier model training against injection.\n   543→                        </div>\n   544→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   545→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n   546→                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-26\n   547→                        </div>\n   548→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   549→                            <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n   550→                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenClaw</span>\n   551→                            <span class=\"tag\">Safety</span>\n   552→                        </div>\n   553→                    </div>\n   554→\n   555→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   556→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   557→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">CVE-2026-LGTM: Satirical Incident</a>\n   558→                        </div>\n   559→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   560→                            Hypothetical incident: competing AI review agents in disagreement loop generate 340 comments and\n   561→                            $41,255 in inference spend before Finance revokes API keys.\n   562→                        </div>\n   563→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   564→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n   565→                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-26\n   566→                        </div>\n   567→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   568→                            <span class=\"tag\">Multi-Agent</span>\n   569→                            <span class=\"tag\">Supply Chain</span>\n   570→                            <span class=\"tag\">Satire</span>\n   571→                        </div>\n   572→                    </div>\n   573→\n   574→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   575→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   576→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27009\" target=\"_blank\">Semantic Early-Stopping for Agent Loops</a>\n   577→                        </div>\n   578→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   579→                            Halts loops when consecutive draft embeddings stop changing in meaning (cosine distance with patience).\n   580→                            Addresses inefficient LLM agent loops continuing without meaningful progress.\n   581→                        </div>\n   582→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   583→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   584→                            Sahil Shrivastava | 2026-06-26\n   585→                        </div>\n   586→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   587→                            <span class=\"tag\">Efficiency</span>\n   588→                            <span class=\"tag\">Early Stopping</span>\n   589→                            <span class=\"tag\">Loops</span>\n   590→                        </div>\n   591→                    </div>\n   592→\n   593→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   594→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   595→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27136\" target=\"_blank\">Experiential Rules & Policies</a>\n   596→                        </div>\n   597→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   598→                            Framework for jointly learning experiential rules and policies. Focus on how agents accumulate and\n   599→                            apply experiential knowledge to improve performance over time.\n   600→                        </div>\n   601→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   602→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   603→                            Shicheng Ye, Chao Yu | 2026-06-26\n   604→                        </div>\n   605→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   606→                            <span class=\"tag\">Learning</span>\n   607→                            <span class=\"tag\">Experience</span>\n   608→                            <span class=\"tag\">Policy</span>\n   609→                        </div>\n   610→                    </div>\n   611→\n   612→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   613→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   614→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27226\" target=\"_blank\">Binary Questions for LLM Evaluation</a>\n   615→                        </div>\n   616→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   617→                            Binary questions instead of judgments for more interpretable LLM evaluation and self-improvement.\n   618→                            Accepted at ICML 2026 Workshop on Compositional Learning.\n   619→                        </div>\n   620→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   621→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   622→                            Sangwoo Cho et al. | 2026-06-26\n   623→                        </div>\n   624→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   625→                            <span class=\"tag\">Evaluation</span>\n   626→                            <span class=\"tag\">Interpretability</span>\n   627→                            <span class=\"tag\">ICML</span>\n   628→                        </div>\n   629→                    </div>\n   630→\n   631→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   632→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   633→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27287\" target=\"_blank\">Prompt Injection in Résumé Screening</a>\n   634→                        </div>\n   635→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   636→                            Analyzes prompt injection vulnerabilities in automated résumé screening. Studies single and multi-injection\n   637→                            attack scenarios. Published in ACL 2026 Findings.\n   638→                        </div>\n   639→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   640→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   641→                            Preet Baxi et al. | 2026-06-26\n   642→                        </div>\n   643→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   644→                            <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n   645→                            <span class=\"tag\">Injection</span>\n   646→                            <span class=\"tag\">ACL</span>\n   647→                        </div>\n   648→                    </div>\n   649→\n   650→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   651→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   652→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26935\" target=\"_blank\">CoT Training Gains in Agents</a>\n   653→                        </div>\n   654→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   655→                            Investigates where Chain-of-Thought training gains manifest in agent systems. Explores disconnect\n   656→                            between training and deployment performance in verbalized CoT.\n   657→                        </div>\n   658→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   659→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   660→                            Jingyu Liu et al. | 2026-06-26\n   661→                        </div>\n   662→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   663→                            <span class=\"tag\">CoT</span>\n   664→                            <span class=\"tag\">Reasoning</span>\n   665→                            <span class=\"tag\">Training</span>\n   666→                        </div>\n   667→                    </div>\n   668→\n   669→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   670→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   671→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26806\" target=\"_blank\">Memory Depth for Long-Running Agents</a>\n   672→                        </div>\n   673→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   674→                            Distinguishes memory access from memory depth. Retrieval for factual access, selective parametric\n   675→                            consolidation for long-running agents.\n   676→                        </div>\n   677→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   678→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   679→                            Haoliang Han | 2026-06-26\n   680→                        </div>\n   681→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   682→                            <span class=\"tag\">Memory</span>\n   683→                            <span class=\"tag\">Consolidation</span>\n   684→                            <span class=\"tag\">Long-Running</span>\n   685→                        </div>\n   686→                    </div>\n   687→\n   688→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   689→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   690→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26649\" target=\"_blank\">Autoformalization to Policy-as-Code</a>\n   691→                        </div>\n   692→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   693→                            Translates agent prompts, MCP tool descriptions, and natural language policy into formalized\n   694→                            policy-as-code. Accepted at ICML 2026 AIWILD Workshop.\n   695→                        </div>\n   696→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   697→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   698→                            Adam Mondl et al. | 2026-06-26\n   699→                        </div>\n   700→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   701→                            <span class=\"tag\">Autoformalization</span>\n   702→                            <span class=\"tag\">Policy</span>\n   703→                            <span class=\"tag\">Safety</span>\n   704→                        </div>\n   705→                    </div>\n   706→\n   707→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   708→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   709→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27288\" target=\"_blank\">Co-Failure Ceiling (67 Models)</a>\n   710→                        </div>\n   711→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   712→                            Studies when combining language models helps through routing, voting, mixture-of-agents.\n   713→                            Identifies 'co-failure ceiling' - limit where combination doesn't improve performance.\n   714→                        </div>\n   715→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   716→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   717→                            Josef Chen | 2026-06-26\n   718→                        </div>\n   719→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   720→                            <span class=\"tag\">Ensemble</span>\n   721→                            <span class=\"tag\">Routing</span>\n   722→                            <span class=\"tag\">67 Models</span>\n   723→                        </div>\n   724→                    </div>\n   725→\n   726→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   727→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   728→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26859\" target=\"_blank\">AgentX for Recommender Systems</a>\n   729→                        </div>\n   730→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   731→                            Agent-driven self-iteration framework for industrial recommender systems. 40+ authors.\n   732→                            Uses agents to continuously improve and adapt recommendation systems.\n   733→                        </div>\n   734→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   735→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   736→                            Changxin Lao et al. | 2026-06-26\n   737→                        </div>\n   738→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   739→                            <span class=\"tag\">Recommender</span>\n   740→                            <span class=\"tag\">Industrial</span>\n   741→                            <span class=\"tag\">Self-Iteration</span>\n   742→                        </div>\n   743→                    </div>\n   744→\n   745→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   746→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   747→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26918\" target=\"_blank\">Diagnosing Task Insensitivity</a>\n   748→                        </div>\n   749→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   750→                            Addresses task insensitivity in language agents - failing to adapt to different task requirements.\n   751→                            Provides diagnostic approaches for understanding task-insensitive behavior.\n   752→                        </div>\n   753→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   754→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   755→                            Jingyu Liu et al. | 2026-06-26\n   756→                        </div>\n   757→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   758→                            <span class=\"tag\">Evaluation</span>\n   759→                            <span class=\"tag\">Task Adaptation</span>\n   760→                        </div>\n   761→                    </div>\n   762→\n   763→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   764→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   765→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26836\" target=\"_blank\">Benchmarks Miss 82% of Performance</a>\n   766→                        </div>\n   767→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   768→                            Current benchmarks fail to capture 82% of model performance. Presents 'capability frontier' framework.\n   769→                        </div>\n   770→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   771→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   772→                            Bradley Fowler et al. | 2026-06-26\n   773→                        </div>\n   774→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   775→                            <span class=\"tag\">Benchmarks</span>\n   776→                            <span class=\"tag\">Evaluation</span>\n   777→                            <span class=\"tag\">Metrics</span>\n   778→                        </div>\n   779→                    </div>\n   780→\n   781→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   782→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   783→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26686\" target=\"_blank\">LeanGuard: Fast Moderation</a>\n   784→                        </div>\n   785→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   786→                            Fast lightweight moderation approach. Questions whether safety guardrails need complex reasoning.\n   787→                            Open-source code/models available.\n   788→                        </div>\n   789→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   790→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   791→                            Dongbin Na | 2026-06-26\n   792→                        </div>\n   793→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   794→                            <span class=\"tag\">Safety</span>\n   795→                            <span class=\"tag\">Moderation</span>\n   796→                            <span class=\"tag\">Efficiency</span>\n   797→                        </div>\n   798→                    </div>\n   799→\n   800→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   801→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   802→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26669\" target=\"_blank\">SKILL-DISCO: Procedural Skills</a>\n   803→                        </div>\n   804→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   805→                            Distills and compiles agent traces into reusable procedural skills. Enables agents to capture and\n   806→                            reuse procedural knowledge from execution traces.\n   807→                        </div>\n   808→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   809→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   810→                            Zhongxin Guo et al. | 2026-06-26\n   811→                        </div>\n   812→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   813→                            <span class=\"tag\">Skills</span>\n   814→                            <span class=\"tag\">Distillation</span>\n   815→                            <span class=\"tag\">Knowledge</span>\n   816→                        </div>\n   817→                    </div>\n   818→\n   819→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   820→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   821→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26722\" target=\"_blank\">Socratic Agents for Discovery</a>\n   822→                        </div>\n   823→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   824→                            Question-driven (Socratic) approaches for autonomous scientific discovery in high-dimensional\n   825→                            physical systems. 27 pages, 5 figures.\n   826→                        </div>\n   827→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   828→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   829→                            Xianrui Zeng et al. | 2026-06-26\n   830→                        </div>\n   831→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   832→                            <span class=\"tag\">Scientific</span>\n   833→                            <span class=\"tag\">Socratic</span>\n   834→                            <span class=\"tag\">Discovery</span>\n   835→                        </div>\n   836→                    </div>\n   837→\n   838→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   839→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   840→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26758\" target=\"_blank\">EGG: Expert-Guided Kernel Generation</a>\n   841→                        </div>\n   842→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   843→                            Expert-guided agent framework for kernel generation. Combines automated agents with expert guidance.\n   844→                        </div>\n   845→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   846→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   847→                            Yaochen Han et al. | 2026-06-26\n   848→                        </div>\n   849→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   850→                            <span class=\"tag\">Kernels</span>\n   851→                            <span class=\"tag\">Code Generation</span>\n   852→                            <span class=\"tag\">Expert-Guided</span>\n   853→                        </div>\n   854→                    </div>\n   855→\n   856→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   857→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   858→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26502\" target=\"_blank\">Humans Disengage, Models Persist</a>\n   859→                        </div>\n   860→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   861→                            Humans disengage from difficult problems, reasoning models persist in deliberation. Separates\n   862→                            difficulty registration from deliberation allocation.\n   863→                        </div>\n   864→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   865→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   866→                            Han-yu Wang | 2026-06-26\n   867→                        </div>\n   868→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   869→                            <span class=\"tag\">Reasoning</span>\n   870→                            <span class=\"tag\">Human-AI</span>\n   871→                            <span class=\"tag\">Deliberation</span>\n   872→                        </div>\n   873→                    </div>\n   874→\n   875→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   876→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   877→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26807\" target=\"_blank\">KARLA: Knowledge-Augmented Retrieval</a>\n   878→                        </div>\n   879→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   880→                            Knowledge-base augmented retrieval for language models. Integrates structured knowledge with retrieval\n   881→                            to improve accuracy and reduce hallucination.\n   882→                        </div>\n   883→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   884→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n   885→                            Francois Crespin et al. | 2026-06-26\n   886→                        </div>\n   887→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   888→                            <span class=\"tag\">RAG</span>\n   889→                            <span class=\"tag\">Knowledge</span>\n   890→                            <span class=\"tag\">Hallucination</span>\n   891→                        </div>\n   892→                    </div>\n   893→\n   894→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   895→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   896→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">German Ruling on Google AI Liability</a>\n   897→                        </div>\n   898→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   899→                            Bruce Schneier on German ruling: Google liable for AI overview errors. AI agents are agents of deploying\n   900→                            organization and should be treated as such by law.\n   901→                        </div>\n   902→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   903→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n   904→                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-25\n   905→                        </div>\n   906→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   907→                            <span class=\"tag\">Liability</span>\n   908→                            <span class=\"tag\">Google</span>\n   909→                            <span class=\"tag\">Law</span>\n   910→                        </div>\n   911→                    </div>\n   912→\n   913→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   914→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   915→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Prompt Injection as Role Confusion</a>\n   916→                        </div>\n   917→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   918→                            Models struggle to distinguish privileged text in role tags from untrusted user input.\n   919→                            'Destyling' text causes attack success to drop from 61% to 10%.\n   920→                        </div>\n   921→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   922→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n   923→                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-22\n   924→                        </div>\n   925→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   926→                            <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n   927→                            <span class=\"tag\">Role Confusion</span>\n   928→                            <span class=\"tag\">Jailbreaking</span>\n   929→                        </div>\n   930→                    </div>\n   931→\n   932→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   933→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   934→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Moebius 0.2B to Browser</a>\n   935→                        </div>\n   936→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   937→                            Ported Moebius 0.2B image inpainting model (PyTorch/CUDA) to browser using WebGPU. 0.2B parameter\n   938→                            model provides 10B-level performance. Demo available.\n   939→                        </div>\n   940→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   941→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n   942→                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-22\n   943→                        </div>\n   944→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   945→                            <span class=\"tag\">WebGPU</span>\n   946→                            <span class=\"tag\">Browser</span>\n   947→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   948→                        </div>\n   949→                    </div>\n   950→\n   951→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   952→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   953→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Cloudflare Temporary Accounts</a>\n   954→                        </div>\n   955→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   956→                            Deploy Workers without account using 'npx wrangler deploy --temporary'. Stay live for 60 minutes.\n   957→                            Marketed 'for AI agents' but interesting for everyone.\n   958→                        </div>\n   959→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   960→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n   961→                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-21\n   962→                        </div>\n   963→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   964→                            <span class=\"tag\">Cloudflare</span>\n   965→                            <span class=\"tag\">Deployment</span>\n   966→                            <span class=\"tag\">Serverless</span>\n   967→                        </div>\n   968→                    </div>\n   969→\n   970→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   971→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   972→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Cloudflare CAPTCHA Optimization</a>\n   973→                        </div>\n   974→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   975→                            Used Claude Code to optimize CAPTCHA rules for faceted search URLs with ampersands.\n   976→                            Tried Cloudflare MCP but couldn't edit rules, switched to API directly.\n   977→                        </div>\n   978→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   979→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n   980→                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-16\n   981→                        </div>\n   982→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   983→                            <span class=\"tag\">Cloudflare</span>\n   984→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   985→                            <span class=\"tag\">MCP</span>\n   986→                        </div>\n   987→                    </div>\n   988→\n   989→                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n   990→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   991→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Fable 5 Export Controls</a>\n   992→                        </div>\n   993→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   994→                            Katie Moussouris: 'Jailbreak' that got Fable 5 banned was simply 'fix this code' on code with CVEs.\n   995→                            'Defenders need to ask AI to fix bugs, explain why, write tests. That's not a bypass - it's the most\n   996→                            valuable thing AI can do for defensive security.'\n   997→                        </div>\n   998→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   999→                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n  1000→                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-16\n  1001→        