       .empty-state {\n            text-align: center;\n            padding: 20px;\n            color: #828282;\n            font-style: italic;\n        }\n\n        /* Footer */\n        footer {\n            background-color: #ffffff;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            padding: 10px;\n            margin-top: 15px;\n            text-align: center;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        footer a {\n            color: #828282;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        footer a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        /* Print styles */\n        @media print {\n            body {\n                background-color: #ffffff;\n            }\n\n            section {\n                border: 1px solid #000000;\n                page-break-inside: avoid;\n            }\n\n            .three-column-layout {\n                display: block;\n            }\n\n            section {\n                margin-bottom: 20px;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Link colors */\n        a {\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        a:hover {\n            color: #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        /* Highlight box for top themes */\n        .highlight-box {\n            background-color: #fff8e6;\n            border: 1px solid #ff6600;\n            padding: 10px;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n        }\n\n        .highlight-box .section-header {\n            border-bottom-color: #ff6600;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <div class=\"header-content\">\n            <div class=\"header-title\">Agentic Coding Research Report</div>\n            <div class=\"header-date\">June 27, 2026</div>\n        </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"header-nav\">\n        <a href=\"#overview\">Overview</a> |\n        <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a> |\n        <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Whitelist Updates</a> |\n        <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Technical Insights</a> |\n        <a href=\"#stats\">Statistics</a>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <main id=\"overview\">\n            <div class=\"highlight-box\">\n                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Top Themes This Week</h2>\n                <div class=\"content-item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">1. GPT-5.6 Launch & Government Access (June 26-27)</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        OpenAI previews GPT-5.6 series: Sol (flagship), Terra (balanced, 2x cheaper), Luna (fast, affordable).\n                        New pricing model with improved prompt caching. U.S. government to control access decisions.\n                        Major Hacker News discussions (831+ points).\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"content-item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">2. Prompt Injection Defense Progress (June 26)</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        6,000 failed hack attempts on OpenClaw challenge. Research shows \"role confusion\" as root vulnerability.\n                        \"Destyling\" attacks reduces success from 61% to 10%. Labs investing in frontier model training against injection.\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"content-item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">3. LLM Agent Research Surge (June 26)</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        17 new ArXiv papers on agent systems. Key topics: semantic early-stopping, experiential learning,\n                        memory consolidation. Autoformalization of agent instructions to policy-as-code.\n                        Co-failure ceiling discovered in model combination (67 models studied).\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"content-item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">4. AI Safety & Regulation (June 16-27)</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Claude Fable 5 export control controversy (defensive security needs). German ruling: Google liable for\n                        AI overview errors. CVE-2026-LGTM satire highlights multi-agent risks. Vibe coding ethics debates on HN.\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"stats-grid\" id=\"stats\">\n                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                    <div class=\"stat-value\">29</div>\n                    <div class=\"stat-label\">Insights Collected</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                    <div class=\"stat-value\">1</div>\n                    <div class=\"stat-label\">New Product</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                    <div class=\"stat-value\">0</div>\n                    <div class=\"stat-label\">Whitelist Updates</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                    <div class=\"stat-value\">17</div>\n                    <div class=\"stat-label\">ArXiv Papers</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                    <div class=\"stat-value\">9</div>\n                    <div class=\"stat-label\">Simon Willison Posts</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                    <div class=\"stat-value\">4</div>\n                    <div class=\"stat-label\">HN Discussions</div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n                <section id=\"new-products\">\n                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">\n                        New Products\n                        <span class=\"section-count\">(1)</span>\n                    </h2>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/lukan-ai-agent-ide-and-workstation\" target=\"_blank\">\n                                Lukan AI Agent, IDE and Workstation\n                            </a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Open-source AI workstation that runs on top of your operating system to complete real end-to-end work.\n                            Includes integrated coding agent (built in Rust), tmux-based persistent terminals, multi-agent parallel\n                            execution, and agentic pipelines with approval workflows.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Product Hunt</span>\n                            Released: 2026-06-23 | Category: AI IDE\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Rust</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Multi-Agent</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenClaw</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Open Source</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\"The pipeline approvals layer is blocking per-agent but async globally\"</div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\"Per-step tool access is underappreciated. Most frameworks give the whole pipeline the same permissions\"</div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\"Persistent memory between sessions - agent barely needs reminding of context\"</div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <section id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">\n                        Whitelist Updates\n                        <span class=\"section-count\">(0)</span>\n                    </h2>\n                    <div class=\"empty-state\">\n                        No whitelist updates recorded for this period.\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <section id=\"technical-insights\">\n                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">\n                        Technical Insights\n                        <span class=\"section-count\">(29)</span>\n                    </h2>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/best\" target=\"_blank\">Hacker News: GPT-5.6 Sol Preview</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            OpenAI's preview of GPT-5.6 Sol as next-generation model. Discussion covers government restrictions\n                            on access - Washington Post reports U.S. government will decide access.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">HN</span>\n                            831 points | 500+ comments | 2026-06-27\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">GPT-5.6</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Government</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/best\" target=\"_blank\">AI Assistant Hack Challenge</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            2,000 people tried to hack Fernando Irarrázaval's AI assistant without success.\n                            Highlights community interest in prompt injection defenses and AI security.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">HN</span>\n                            351 points | 158 comments | 2026-06-27\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Prompt Injection</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenClaw</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/best\" target=\"_blank\">CVE-2026-LGTM Incident</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Andrew Nesbitt's satirical AI security incident about competing AI agents entering disagreement loops.\n                            519 points, 83 comments. Highlights multi-agent concerns and inference costs.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">HN</span>\n                            519 points | 83 comments | 2026-06-27\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Multi-Agent</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Satire</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Incident Response</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/best\" target=\"_blank\">Vibe Coding Controversy</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Discussion about code attribution and ethics of AI-generated code. \"Hey Nico, you didn't vibe code your\n                            data room but stole it from Papermark.\" 590 points, 275 comments.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">HN</span>\n                            590 points | 275 comments | 2026-06-27\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Ethics</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Attribution</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Vibe Coding</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">GPT-5.6 Preview and Pricing</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Three models: Sol (flagship), Terra (2x cheaper), Luna (fast/affordable). Pricing: Sol $5/$30 per 1M tokens,\n                            Terra $2.50/$15, Luna $1/$6. Predictable prompt caching with 30-min cache life.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">GPT-5.6</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Pricing</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Caching</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Prompt Injection Defense Progress</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            6,000 attempts to leak OpenClaw secrets using Opus 4.6 - zero successes. Anti-prompt-injection rules\n                            and training appear effective. Labs investing in frontier model training against injection.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenClaw</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Safety</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">CVE-2026-LGTM: Satirical Incident</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Hypothetical incident: competing AI review agents in disagreement loop generate 340 comments and\n                            $41,255 in inference spend before Finance revokes API keys.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Multi-Agent</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Supply Chain</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Satire</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27009\" target=\"_blank\">Semantic Early-Stopping for Agent Loops</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Halts loops when consecutive draft embeddings stop changing in meaning (cosine distance with patience).\n                            Addresses inefficient LLM agent loops continuing without meaningful progress.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Sahil Shrivastava | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Efficiency</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Early Stopping</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Loops</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27136\" target=\"_blank\">Experiential Rules & Policies</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Framework for jointly learning experiential rules and policies. Focus on how agents accumulate and\n                            apply experiential knowledge to improve performance over time.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Shicheng Ye, Chao Yu | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Learning</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Experience</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Policy</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27226\" target=\"_blank\">Binary Questions for LLM Evaluation</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Binary questions instead of judgments for more interpretable LLM evaluation and self-improvement.\n                            Accepted at ICML 2026 Workshop on Compositional Learning.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Sangwoo Cho et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Evaluation</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Interpretability</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ICML</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27287\" target=\"_blank\">Prompt Injection in Résumé Screening</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Analyzes prompt injection vulnerabilities in automated résumé screening. Studies single and multi-injection\n                            attack scenarios. Published in ACL 2026 Findings.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Preet Baxi et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Injection</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">ACL</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26935\" target=\"_blank\">CoT Training Gains in Agents</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Investigates where Chain-of-Thought training gains manifest in agent systems. Explores disconnect\n                            between training and deployment performance in verbalized CoT.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Jingyu Liu et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">CoT</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Reasoning</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Training</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26806\" target=\"_blank\">Memory Depth for Long-Running Agents</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Distinguishes memory access from memory depth. Retrieval for factual access, selective parametric\n                            consolidation for long-running agents.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Haoliang Han | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Memory</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Consolidation</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Long-Running</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26649\" target=\"_blank\">Autoformalization to Policy-as-Code</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Translates agent prompts, MCP tool descriptions, and natural language policy into formalized\n                            policy-as-code. Accepted at ICML 2026 AIWILD Workshop.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Adam Mondl et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Autoformalization</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Policy</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Safety</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.27288\" target=\"_blank\">Co-Failure Ceiling (67 Models)</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Studies when combining language models helps through routing, voting, mixture-of-agents.\n                            Identifies 'co-failure ceiling' - limit where combination doesn't improve performance.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Josef Chen | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Ensemble</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Routing</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">67 Models</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26859\" target=\"_blank\">AgentX for Recommender Systems</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Agent-driven self-iteration framework for industrial recommender systems. 40+ authors.\n                            Uses agents to continuously improve and adapt recommendation systems.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Changxin Lao et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Recommender</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Industrial</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Self-Iteration</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26918\" target=\"_blank\">Diagnosing Task Insensitivity</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Addresses task insensitivity in language agents - failing to adapt to different task requirements.\n                            Provides diagnostic approaches for understanding task-insensitive behavior.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Jingyu Liu et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Evaluation</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Task Adaptation</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26836\" target=\"_blank\">Benchmarks Miss 82% of Performance</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Current benchmarks fail to capture 82% of model performance. Presents 'capability frontier' framework.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Bradley Fowler et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Benchmarks</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Evaluation</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Metrics</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26686\" target=\"_blank\">LeanGuard: Fast Moderation</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Fast lightweight moderation approach. Questions whether safety guardrails need complex reasoning.\n                            Open-source code/models available.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Dongbin Na | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Safety</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Moderation</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Efficiency</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26669\" target=\"_blank\">SKILL-DISCO: Procedural Skills</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Distills and compiles agent traces into reusable procedural skills. Enables agents to capture and\n                            reuse procedural knowledge from execution traces.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Zhongxin Guo et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Skills</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Distillation</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Knowledge</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26722\" target=\"_blank\">Socratic Agents for Discovery</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Question-driven (Socratic) approaches for autonomous scientific discovery in high-dimensional\n                            physical systems. 27 pages, 5 figures.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Xianrui Zeng et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Scientific</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Socratic</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Discovery</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26758\" target=\"_blank\">EGG: Expert-Guided Kernel Generation</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Expert-guided agent framework for kernel generation. Combines automated agents with expert guidance.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Yaochen Han et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Kernels</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Code Generation</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Expert-Guided</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26502\" target=\"_blank\">Humans Disengage, Models Persist</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Humans disengage from difficult problems, reasoning models persist in deliberation. Separates\n                            difficulty registration from deliberation allocation.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Han-yu Wang | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Reasoning</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Human-AI</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Deliberation</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26807\" target=\"_blank\">KARLA: Knowledge-Augmented Retrieval</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Knowledge-base augmented retrieval for language models. Integrates structured knowledge with retrieval\n                            to improve accuracy and reduce hallucination.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Paper</span>\n                            Francois Crespin et al. | 2026-06-26\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">RAG</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Knowledge</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Hallucination</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">German Ruling on Google AI Liability</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Bruce Schneier on German ruling: Google liable for AI overview errors. AI agents are agents of deploying\n                            organization and should be treated as such by law.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-25\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Liability</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Google</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Law</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Prompt Injection as Role Confusion</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Models struggle to distinguish privileged text in role tags from untrusted user input.\n                            'Destyling' text causes attack success to drop from 61% to 10%.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-22\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Role Confusion</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Jailbreaking</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Moebius 0.2B to Browser</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Ported Moebius 0.2B image inpainting model (PyTorch/CUDA) to browser using WebGPU. 0.2B parameter\n                            model provides 10B-level performance. Demo available.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-22\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">WebGPU</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Browser</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Cloudflare Temporary Accounts</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Deploy Workers without account using 'npx wrangler deploy --temporary'. Stay live for 60 minutes.\n                            Marketed 'for AI agents' but interesting for everyone.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-21\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Cloudflare</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Deployment</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Serverless</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Cloudflare CAPTCHA Optimization</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Used Claude Code to optimize CAPTCHA rules for faceted search URLs with ampersands.\n                            Tried Cloudflare MCP but couldn't edit rules, switched to API directly.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-16\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Cloudflare</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">MCP</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Fable 5 Export Controls</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Katie Moussouris: 'Jailbreak' that got Fable 5 banned was simply 'fix this code' on code with CVEs.\n                            'Defenders need to ask AI to fix bugs, explain why, write tests. That's not a bypass - it's the most\n                            valuable thing AI can do for defensive security.'\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"source-indicator\">Blog</span>\n                            Simon Willison | 2026-06-16\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"tags\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Export Controls</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Fable 5</span>\n                            <span class=\"tag\">Cyberdefense</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n            </div>\n        </main>\n\n        <footer>\n            <p>\n                Generated on June 27, 2026 | Sources: Simon Willison, ArXiv, Hacker News, Product Hunt |\n                <a href=\"#\">Top</a>\n            </p>\n        </footer>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>",
